    "body": "Bamboo17 intentionally rejects a mode-free first browser open on Linux and Windows. A closed browser with no profile report now offers a separate user-selected clean action and sends `profile_mode: clean`; the default request remains unchanged. Only a coherent server ACK can report the clean mode. Session fencing, pending-request fencing and unknown-result handling remain intact.\n\nReal Bamboo acceptance clicks this visible clean action from a genuinely closed browser. Shared tabs, epoch, screenshots, model control and negative profile assertions remain unchanged. CI checkout now explicitly selects the PR head, reusing #433's source-binding expression without adding sharding or changing the job graph.\n\nCurrent head: `5981217656e330bbb06e02b32cfcc2989501cb2f`; source tree `750311019904d48610caffb560c4f063d6294935`. Code review completed with no findings. Exact-head CI: https://github.com/bigduu/lotus-next/actions/runs/40216330233 (Node22/24 basic verification passed; browser suites in progress).\n\nLocal validation of unchanged product code: 38 focused unit tests and 5 browser-profile flows passed; TypeScript, lint, i18n and production build passed. The full unit run had 4815 passing assertions but exited 1 because an unchanged ProviderSettings timer fired after JSDOM teardown (`DefaultsEditor.tsx:308`); its isolated 39 tests passed, and the original error is retained.\n\nLocal real Bamboo17 attempt: 0 passed / 1 failed, exit 1. The trace stops at initial page GET / without a response; no browser PUT was issued. Docker cleanup reported the harness-owned main PID as zombie and could not remove that container and its dedicated network. This attempt does not prove clean opening and is not counted as acceptance. The normal Linux release artifact gate remains required.\n\nThe candidate excludes later #430/#427 product changes. The prior synthetic-merge CI 40215054467 was cancelled by existing concurrency policy after the checkout correction and is not claimed as exact-source acceptance. The failed immutable 2026.10.25 candidate and publication evidence remain unchanged.",
